sparky-stereo-camera 0.1.0 (2026-11-15)
  * First release (ORDER 570): the Camera page of System Settings, under Multimedia beside Sound.
  * The default camera is WirePlumber's default.configured.video.source; format, size and frame rate and the camera's own controls are set on the V4L2 device and kept in ~/.config/sparky-stereo-camera/cameras.ini; a user service applies them again when a camera is plugged in.
  * A live preview from PipeWire; a two-lens camera is given its packing (the stereo layer's list) and its pair is shown as a declared full side by side picture.
  * Every refusal, a held camera, no camera and a failed preview are said on the page; ten languages.
